cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Still True or its evaluation, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Still True: re-checks every scheduled Buffer post against the world just before it goes out"
abstract: >-
  Still True reads a Buffer queue again just before each post goes out and checks it against the
  calendar, the linked product and event pages, the weather forecast, national remembrance days, GDACS
  disaster alerts and Wikipedia's Current Events. Deterministic rules decide; posts the world has made
  wrong are moved to drafts and explained inside Buffer. Evaluated on 410 labelled cases written before
  the code and on five real days.
authors:
